    "citations": null,
    "text": "{\"completeness\": 0.85, \"citation_quality\": 0.75, \"severity_defensibility\": 0.80, \"overall_pass\": true, \"feedback\": \"This is a solid triage that correctly identifies a blocked brute force attempt and appropriately scopes it as medium severity. The investigation could be strengthened by: (1) explicitly addressing the confidence score of 0.0 and explaining why identity signals are absent (e.g., clarifying whether this is expected for perimeter blocks), (2) providing more specific justification for why T1078 Valid Accounts applies here\u2014the evidence primarily supports T1110 variants, and T1078 typically requires successful account compromise or misuse, (3) noting the number of attempts (3) in relation to your account lockout policy recommendations to show they align, and (4) adding one concrete metric or threshold that would trigger escalation (e.g., 'if 10+ failures occur in 5 minutes from multiple sources' or 'if any authentication succeeds'). Overall, the defensive posture and severity calibration are sound and proportionate to the threat.\"}",
    "type": "text"
   }
  ],
