  "content": [
   {
    "citations": null,
    "text": "{\"attack_techniques\":[{\"id\":\"T1110.001\",\"name\":\"Password Guessing\",\"tactics\":[\"Credential Access\"],\"why_relevant\":\"The alert shows failed Kerberos authentication with invalid credentials on username rthompson after 3 attempts, consistent with an adversary guessing passwords against known accounts.\"},{\"id\":\"T1110\",\"name\":\"Brute Force\",\"tactics\":[\"Credential Access\"],\"why_relevant\":\"Multiple failed authentication attempts (attempt=3) using the Kerberos method against a specific username indicates potential brute force activity to compromise account credentials.\"},{\"id\":\"T1078\",\"name\":\"Valid Accounts\",\"tactics\":[\"Stealth\",\"Persistence\",\"Privilege Escalation\",\"Initial Access\"],\"why_relevant\":\"The alert targets a valid account (rthompson) which, if compromised through repeated failed login attempts, could be abused for initial access or persistence.\"}],\"identity_signals\":{\"impossible_travel\":false,\"mfa_fatigue\":false,\"privilege_escalation\":false,\"dormant_account_reactivation\":false,\"notes\":\"No identity signals detected. No anomalous sign-in patterns, privilege escalation, or account reactivation observed.\"},\"key_findings\":\"Failed Kerberos authentication attempt against valid account rthompson from external IP 198.51.100.88 after 3 invalid credential attempts suggests brute force or password guessing activity. No evidence of successful compromise or internal impact detected, and no anomalous identity signals such as impossible travel or MFA fatigue were observed. The attack was denied at the perimeter with no indication that authentication controls were bypassed.\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"severity_rationale\":\"This is an external attack attempt against the perimeter that was stopped by authentication controls\u2014the failed attempts demonstrate the system rejected invalid credentials and the account has not been compromised. There is no evidence of lateral movement, persistence, malware execution, or any internal host or account impact. The brute force activity represents a common attack pattern that was successfully blocked, meeting the definition of medium severity.\",\"confidence\":0.78,\"recommended_response\":\"Monitor the rthompson account for any successful authentication from this or similar sources. Verify that account lockout policies are enforced and tuned appropriately. Consider adding 198.51.100.88 to threat intelligence blocklists if the source is confirmed malicious. Routine monitoring of this account should continue, but no immediate escalation is required unless additional suspicious activity occurs.\",\"rounds_used\":0}",
    "type": "text"
   }
  ],
